  "id": "COMPOUND:307 - PROTEIN:4285",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that gefitinib may interact with Alpha-2-antiplasmin through multiple distinct mechanisms, each involving different targets. The drug is known to target Ephrin type-A receptor 6, which is a substrate of Sinocalycanchinensin G, and this pathway ultimately leads to the inhibition of Alpha-2-antiplasmin. Similarly, gefitinib also targets Serine/threonine-protein kinase TAO1, which is a target of K-252a, another compound that inhibits Alpha-2-antiplasmin. Additionally, gefitinib interacts with Transmembrane glycoprotein NMB, which is a target of flavopiridol, another inhibitor of Alpha-2-antiplasmin. These findings collectively indicate that gefitinib may exert its effects on Alpha-2-antiplasmin through different molecular pathways, each of which is supported by the presence of specific inhibitors. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the drug-target relationship and underscores the importance of understanding the underlying mechanisms to predict and optimize therapeutic outcomes.",
